+# Seasons 19-30 compatibility - candidate 1
+
+This package enables existing Erbium paths over game releases 19.xx-30.xx,
+with engine version 5.0-5.5. Engine and game versions are parsed independently.
+This is an experimental target range, not a list of verified playable builds.
+
+| Game release range | Battle Royale map | Implementation status |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| 19.xx-22.xx | Artemis_Terrain | Existing Erbium map/native paths enabled |
+| 23.xx-26.xx | Asteria_Terrain | Existing Erbium map/native paths enabled |
+| 27.xx | Athena_Terrain | Earlier 27.11 path retained and neighboring releases enabled |
+| 28.xx-30.xx | Helios_Terrain | Existing Erbium map/native paths enabled |
+
+Both DLLs use the same profile. UE5 builds below 5.3 use the existing legacy
+replication path; UE5.3 and later use the existing Iris path unless explicitly
+disabled in shared configuration. The Season 29+ Iris inventory-filter path
+now checks that its configuration object/property exists before accessing it.
+Missing required core bindings, including the FName constructor, stop SDK
+initialization with diagnostics rather than being treated as compatible.
+
+The shared reflection profile preserves upstream's layout boundaries at 20.00,
+20.20 and 24.30. It does not invent offsets for unknown executables. All other
+engine-specific finders, hooks and gameplay paths remain from the pinned base.
+Neither a nonzero signature match nor accepting a version string proves that
+an address has the right ABI or that all hooks/gameplay features work.
+
+Upstream documents support through 19.40 and partial support from 20.00 through
+30.00. Later 30.xx releases are selectable but receive an additional diagnostic
+because they exceed that documented endpoint. See
+[upstream README](https://github.com/plooshi/Erbium/tree/44568e08cbe411ba197d3e0e900685750d46afdc).
+
+## What is known from the earlier 27.11 attempt
+
+The authentication candidate allowed lobby login. ProcessEvent resolved, and
+one earlier host log recorded a player joining. A later connection timed out;
+the paired host log ended before the client connected. A host crash was also
+reported without a matching crash dump. A complete match was not verified.
+None of the new Seasons 19-30 DLLs has yet been run against a Fortnite executable.
+
+## Verification provided with this candidate
+
+- Parser/profile checks cover all twelve seasons, exact game/engine separation,
+  patch-boundary reflection layouts, map selection, matching Iris policy,
+  out-of-range versions, malformed labels and numeric overflow.
+- Windows ProcessEvent lookup tests exercise the existing lookup safeguards.
+- Windows authentication tests cover scanners and synthetic hook/URL behavior.
+- The CI build validates all three binaries as AMD64 PE32+ DLLs with entry points.
+- The pinned backend is queried using all twelve season identifiers for discovery,
+  profiles and local matchmaking. Those HTTP checks use synthetic user agents;
+  they do not run the Fortnite clients.
+
+The artifact's BUILD-INFO.txt identifies the actual completed build. Gameplay,
+player replication, vehicles, movement workarounds, stability and complete matches
+remain unverified across this range. Special events, Creative, Save the World,
+XP/quests and persistence are outside this Battle Royale candidate's validation.
